simplify: \frac{3x+2}{x-1}=4
Multiply both sides of the equation by (x-1) to eliminate the denominator:
$$ \begin{align*} 
(3x+2) &= 4(x - 1) \\
3x + 2 &= 4x - 4 \\
2 + 4 &= 4x - 3x \\
6 &= x
\end{align*} $$

Therefore, the solution is $\boxed{6}$.
The solution is $\boxed{6}$. 

